@startuml cloning_transaction
skinparam BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam maxMessageSize 78
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam sequence {
    ArrowColor #0D47A1
    LifeLineBorderColor #1565C0
    LifeLineBackgroundColor #E3F2FD
    ParticipantBorderColor #1565C0
    ParticipantBackgroundColor #E3F2FD
    ParticipantFontColor #000000
    DatabaseBorderColor #2E7D32
    DatabaseBackgroundColor #E8F5E9
    DatabaseFontColor #000000
    BoxBorderColor #616161
    BoxBackgroundColor #FAFAFA
}
skinparam note {
    BackgroundColor #FFF9C4
    BorderColor #F9A825
    FontColor #000000
}
hide footbox

title AX Cross-Environment Clone — Transaction and Lineage Flow

actor Operator

box "Executing AX Host" #FAFAFA
participant "Clone Controller" as Core
collections "Fresh Isolated\nObject Sinks" as Sinks
database "Host-Local AX Store\nJournal 3 + Bundle Chain" as AXStore
end box

box "Source Host" #FAFAFA
participant "Source Session Adapter 1.0\n(trusted ax-provider executable)" as Source
database "Source Host-Local\nNative Store" as SourceStore
end box

box "Target Host" #FAFAFA
participant "Target Session Adapter 1.0\n(trusted ax-provider executable)" as Target
participant "Target Provider 2.0\n(transaction authority)" as Provider
database "Target Host-Local\nNative Store + Rollback State" as TargetStore
participant "Native Target CLI" as TargetCLI
end box

autonumber

== Resolve, bind, and prove a stable source ==

Operator -> Core: ax session clone run SOURCE --from-provider A --to-provider B
Core -> Source: manifest + probe + inspect (read authority)
Source -> SourceStore: discover exact native identity and store generation
Source --> Core: source basis + exact observed execution binding
Core -> Target: manifest + probe exact target tuple and capabilities
Target --> Core: exact observed target execution binding
Core -> AXStore: persist Journal 3 snapshotting\n(two immutable adapter bindings + source basis)
Core -> Source: snapshot-proof(expected generation)
Source -> SourceStore: prove closed store / snapshot / log prefix / quiescence

alt Stable boundary unavailable
    Source --> Core: fail-closed evidence
    Core --> Operator: failure; no target object or native-store mutation
else Stable source proven
    Source --> Core: stable proof + generation + equal pre/post digests
end

== Capture, normalize, and plan in isolated authority ==

Core -> Source: capture-plan + capture (fresh bounded sinks)
Source -> SourceStore: read allowlisted durable native items
Source -> Sinks: raw objects + Capture Manifest candidates
Core -> Core: reconcile, validate, rehash, and seal candidates
Core -> AXStore: persist G0 capture
Core -> Source: normalize(raw authority, fresh canonical sink)
Source -> Sinks: Canonical Session + ordered Canonical Events
Core -> Core: validate graph, evidence closure, IDs, and policy inputs
Core -> AXStore: persist G1 canonical

Core -> Target: projection-plan + project (fresh target-object sink)
Target -> Sinks: Projection Plan + Projected Object Manifest candidates
Core -> Core: enforce per-item fidelity policy and target limits

alt Required fidelity cannot be met
    Core --> Operator: fail before target mutation; retain G0–G1
else Projection accepted
    Core -> Target: staged read-back + validate over isolated projected objects
    Target -> Sinks: staged evidence (identity/workspace/markers/resume surface)
    Core -> AXStore: persist Plan 2 + Migration Checkpoint + G2\nand Journal prepared
end

== Publish with Provider-owned rollback ==

Core -> Source: recheck source generation before Provider materialize
Source -> SourceStore: read unchanged generation/digest
Source --> Core: prepublication source check
break Prepublication source changed
    Core -> AXStore: persist failure; retain G0–G2
    Core --> Operator: source_changed; no Provider or target mutation
end
Core -> Provider: materialize(Plan 2, projected objects,\nhost-created transaction authority)
Provider -> TargetStore: publish exact new native identity\nwhile retaining rollback state
Provider --> Core: prepared + rollback token + native discovery proof
Core -> AXStore: persist Journal published + prepared-result fact

Core -> Source: postpublication source generation recheck
Source -> SourceStore: read generation/digest again
Source --> Core: postpublication source check
Core -> Target: live read-back exact target identity
Target -> TargetStore: independently parse inert published target
Target -> Sinks: live evidence
Core -> Target: validate live evidence + resume-plan(existing identity)
Target --> Core: validation facts + explicit resume argv
Core -> Provider: capture exact published native identity
Provider -> TargetStore: capture ordinary live Provider Transfer Manifest\nwhile rollback remains retained
Provider --> Core: ordinary live Provider Transfer Manifest

alt Source check, live validation, or Provider capture fails
    Core -> AXStore: persist rolling_back intent
    Core -> Provider: materialize-rollback(same transaction authority)
    Provider -> TargetStore: restore predecessor / remove introduced identity
    Provider --> Core: rolled_back; rollback token cleared
    Core -> AXStore: persist rolled_back; retain highest verified G0–G3 evidence
    Core --> Operator: failure report; no target activation
else Live validation passes
    Core -> AXStore: persist Fidelity + Validation Reports + G3\nand Journal finalizing intent
    Core -> Provider: materialize-commit(activation=dormant_validated)
    Provider -> TargetStore: commit exact identity and discard rollback state
    Provider --> Core: committed result (rollback token null)
    Core -> AXStore: persist provider_committed fact
end

note over Core,Provider
  After Provider commit, byte rollback is forbidden.
  Recovery may only complete the same deterministic suffix or park input-blocked.
end note

== Seal target authority, then publish lineage ==

Core -> Target: read-back + validate exact closed committed target
Target -> TargetStore: independently prove identity, full idle,\ninput blocked, zero processes/handles
Target --> Core: post-commit revalidation evidence
Core -> AXStore: seal epoch-1 target Checkpoint
Core -> AXStore: emit checkpoint.created, then clone.committed
Core -> AXStore: publish Lineage Receipt, then G4 committed bundle

opt Open requested after lineage publication
    Core -> TargetCLI: resume explicit existing TARGET_ID
    TargetCLI -> TargetStore: open committed native identity
end

Core --> Operator: target ID + resume argv + fidelity/validation + lineage receipt

note over Source,Target
  Each environment has one companion Session Adapter.
  Canonical contracts bridge them; there is no A×B converter matrix.
end note

@enduml
